## Description

This detection identifies **Windows Security Event ID 5379**, which is generated when **Credential Manager credentials are read**.

Credential Manager stores usernames, passwords, certificates, and other authentication secrets used by Windows and applications. Adversaries often attempt to access stored credentials after gaining access to a system in order to escalate privileges, move laterally, or maintain persistence.

Monitoring Event ID 5379 helps defenders identify potential credential access activity and investigate unauthorized attempts to retrieve stored credentials.

