# Analyst Notes

Credential theft remains one of the primary objectives following initial compromise. Windows Credential Manager can contain cached credentials used for Remote Desktop, network shares, web applications, and enterprise services.

Although legitimate software may access stored credentials, unexpected Credential Manager activity should always be investigated, particularly when combined with PowerShell execution, encoded commands, administrative logons, or other post-exploitation techniques.

This detection provides valuable visibility into potential credential harvesting attempts and strengthens the overall endpoint detection strategy within the Splunk Home Lab.
